<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hyōgo Prefecture</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hyōgo Prefecture is a prefecture of the Kansai region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reaching from the Inland Sea to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kobe">Kobe</a>. It was formed in the 1870s from parts of the old provinces of Settsu, Harima, Tajima, Tamba and Awaji. It contains Himeji Castle, a World Heritage Site since 1993, and was struck by the Great Hanshin earthquake in 1995.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hyogo-prefecture.jpg" alt="Hyōgo Prefecture" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Laitr Keiows · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Night_view_of_Rokk%C5%8D_Island_and_Higashinada-ku,_Kobe,_Japan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
